security, in each case, as the Agent or such Secured Party in its discretion may determine consistent herewith, with the Note Purchase Agreement and with any applicable security agreement, including foreclosure on any such security pursuant to one
or more judicial or nonjudicial sales, whether or not every aspect of any such sale is commercially reasonable, and even though such action operates to impair or extinguish any right of reimbursement or subrogation or other right or remedy of any
Guarantor against any Note Party or any security for the Obligations; and (vi)&nbsp;exercise any other rights available to it under the Note Documents or at Law; and </P>
 <p STYLE="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&nbsp;</P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="center">8 </P>

